{
  "id": "mark-vs-wiggle-bigwig",
  "measured": "2026-09-28",
  "published": false,
  "source": {
    "kind": "bench",
    "repro": "node --experimental-transform-types plugins/marks/benches/bigwigPaths.bench.ts --json, then the same with --file=<a coverage BigWig> --start=10000000 for the second file (CD16_Mono.bw is a 10x scRNA cluster coverage track over hg38, copied to ~/data on ada)",
    "notes": "On ada (24 cores, load ~4). One 1500 px screen per zoom, from the contig start, at one bp/px inside each of the file's tiers, the adapter's synthetic tiers included (ADR-129), and one in its raw section; `tier` is the reduction level the adapter reads at that zoom. wiggle is getFeatureArraysMulti plus processFeaturesFromArrays, the RenderWiggleData executor's work for the region; marks is getFeaturesArray plus encodeFeatures over the bar shape's lanes, the CoreGetEncodedLayers executor's work for `{ mark: 'bar', encoding: { y: 'score' } }`, so the difference is the BigWigFeature objects and the rxjs collect; marks-mean runs `bin: auto` and `aggregate: mean` on top. The weighted arm is getFeatureTable through `bin: auto` over `fields: ['start', 'end']` and `aggregate: mean` of score weighted by `overlap` (ADR-197). control is the wiggle arm declared a second time. MIN across rounds, bbi's block cache warm after the first round: a refetch across a tier, not a cold open. The error columns are against the raw section's coverage-weighted mean over the same bins, as a percentage of the raw score range on the screen: the mean-of-means is `bin: auto` by start and an unweighted mean, each tier row in its start's bin; the weighted column is the weighted arm's answer, each tier row cut at the bin edges."
  },
